* Bug 1: stale en-passant state after make/unmake
  (description generated by gpt)
  applyMoveImpure is reversible: applying the same pieceMovement again is used
  to unmake the move. This requires each generated move to encode the board's
  current en-passant state so that the metadata is restored correctly during
  unmake.

  One move-generation helper initialized the move's enPassantState to -1 instead
  of board.enPassantState. As a result, piece placement was restored correctly
  after make/unmake, but the en-passant metadata could become stale. Perftree
  then generated 1-2 illegal extra en-passant captures in some branches.

  This did not reproduce by loading the later FEN directly, because the bug was
  not in move generation from a clean position. It only appeared after a
  make/unmake sequence created a board with correct pieces but incorrect
  en-passant state.

  Incorrect:
  @code cpp
  int8_t enPassantState {-1};
  @end

  Correct:
  @code cpp
  int8_t enPassantState {board.enPassantState};
  @end

  Location:
  addAttacksToStack218(...)

  Regression test:
  TODO

  Fixed in:
  TODO
  ---
* bug2
  attacks by enemy sliding pieces prevent longside castling when they should not, if white is castling long and blacks piece attacks the b1 square then white cannot castle

  change 
  uint64_t black_squares_to_check_empty_long_castle = 0xe;
  to 
  uint64_t black_squares_to_check_empty_long_castle = 0xc;
  #TODO add bitboard visualisation here
  ---

* bug3 
  last bugfix introduced a new bug!
  we can castle through our own pieces if they are on the b1 square, since we changed the mask to not include the b1 square, we now need two bitbmask instead of one 

  split this statement into 
  @code lang
  !((isWhiteTurn ? black_squares_to_check_empty_long_castle << 56 : black_squares_to_check_empty_long_castle) & (all_pieces | enemy_attacks.value())
  @end
  into
  @code lang
  !((isWhiteTurn ? black_squares_to_check_empty_long_castle << 56 : black_squares_to_check_empty_long_castle) & (all_pieces)) &&  
  !((isWhiteTurn ? black_square_to_check_not_attacked << 56 : black_square_to_check_not_attacked) & (enemy_attacks.value())
  @end
  where
  @code lang
  
 uint64_t black_square_to_check_not_attacked= 0xc;
 uint64_t black_squares_to_check_empty_long_castle = 0xe;
  @end


* state of bugs
  Perftree traverses the generated move tree and compares our generated moves to a mature move generator (the move gen which is a component of stockfish)
  when running perftree at depth 6 on move 13 of Rotlewi vs. Rubinstein, Lodz 1907 with fen of "r1b2rk1/4qppp/p1nbpn2/1p6/1PB5/P1N1PN2/1B1Q1PPP/R3K2R w KQ b6 0 13"
  each of the 6,492,889,510 leaf nodes (moves) generated by our engine matches the moves generated by stockfish 
  perftree testing of more positions is required to become more confident in movegen correctness. 
  Some of the obvious cases of movegen incorrectness have been caught, although there are probably many more edge cases that will need to be found by 
  running perftree on randomly sampled chess postitions.

  TODO : write automated test cases / regression tests
